WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.709 --> 00:00:02.836
Rodrigo told me
he had this new script.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.671
And then I was
slightly blown away

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.964
by the actual script itself

00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:08.091
'cause it's a really
interesting story.

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:08.967
Really?

00:00:09.468 --> 00:00:11.720
The cheapest man
who ever lived.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.890
It's as old as time,
the stories of fathers and sons.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.100
The brothers are here
very reluctantly.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.143
They are half brothers.

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:19.686
They both share this father

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.522
and he was a terrible
father to them.

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:23.315
They haven't
even seen him in years

00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:25.400
and they hear that his
last wish is that they

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.318
dig his grave.

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:28.654
And then, you are to
lower the casket

00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:29.863
and cover the grave again.

00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:31.448
What?

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:32.824
[director]
And action!

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:34.076
Ethan and I...

00:00:34.076 --> 00:00:35.285
I always thought
that we would

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:36.328
end up
in a movie together

00:00:36.328 --> 00:00:38.372
but it's taken like
30 years for that to happen.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:39.957
So it was lovely to

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:42.209
finally get a chance
to work together to--

00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:44.378
throw ourselves into
these incredible scenes.

00:00:44.378 --> 00:00:47.381
His last wish was that his
sons attend his funeral.

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:48.465
You don't have to go.

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:50.425
He's dead.

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:51.969
He'll never know.

00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:54.930
You are a very tender man,
you know that?

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:56.640
The humor

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.100
and vulnerability

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.434
of these brothers

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:00.686
it really moved me.

00:01:00.686 --> 00:01:01.520
Hi.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.188
How did you know our father?

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:04.982
We were lovers for awhile.

00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:07.526
[director]
Action.

00:01:07.526 --> 00:01:09.611
This film explores
human nature.

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:11.363
That's why it hits you
in such a deep way.

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:14.658
It's moving and true,
and very funny.

00:01:14.658 --> 00:01:15.909
What was he like as a father?

00:01:17.411 --> 00:01:18.245
The worst.

00:01:18.245 --> 00:01:20.247
Your father's wish was
to be buried naked.

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:21.373
Why is he faced down?

00:01:21.373 --> 00:01:22.833
It's what he requested.

00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:23.667
I got it.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.878
The best movies
start at the end.

00:01:26.587 --> 00:01:28.255
You know as you're
walking out of the theater

00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:30.591
when a movie starts
vibrating inside your head

00:01:30.591 --> 00:01:32.676
with how it relates
to your own life.

00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:34.636
I hope it's a movie
that rings that bell

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:36.763
that sounds long after
it's been rung.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.140
- Pull over!
- I like you and--

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.224
- Whoa, whoa.
- Hey!

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:40.225
♪♪

